**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** The naming template becomes a field of the kit file, stored as the text the lab writes (001 §J 'Naming template: each kit carries one (e.g. `{source}-({obj1}#{phi1}-{obj2}#{phi2})-{analyzer}-{note}`)'; 001 §A 'the kit: id, name, author, notes, naming template, import profiles, sendExclude'; step 122: 'S8.3 adds the naming template'). The grammar, the reading and the writing are steps 268-271's; this step adds the stored shape and its default. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.3. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs`, directly before `KitFile` (step 122): `NamingTemplate of string` with `.value`, the kit's naming template as its text, and `static member standard : NamingTemplate`, which is `NamingTemplate "{source}-({obj1}#{phi1}-{obj2}#{phi2})-{analyzer}-{note}"`: 001 §J's template, the one place that text is written, every new kit's template and the grammar of the reference pipeline's labels (step 270). It is not validated here: the grammar is `NamingTemplates.fs`'s (step 268), and every use of a template answers a `Result`. (2) `KitFile` gains `namingTemplate : NamingTemplate` after `sendExclude`, and `KitFile.create` sets it to `NamingTemplate.standard`, so `KitFolder.namedKitFile` (step 145) and `scratchKit` (step 150), which call `create`, take it with no change. The shared serializer options unwrap a single-case union (`ProjectJson.fs:142`, `WithUnionUnwrapSingleCaseUnions`, moved into `CanonicalJson.fs` by step 21), so the template is written as a JSON string. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/kit.schema.json` (step 124): under `if` `schemaVersion` is 1, `namingTemplate` joins the required keys and the properties as a string, and `additionalProperties: false` stays. The schema version stays 1: kit files of the old shape exist only under test output folders (.spec-md §7: kit file shapes change in later parts and no migration is needed). No up-converter, default-on-read or other member is added. Tests. In `KitTests` (step 122): `a kit's naming template keeps its text, and a new kit takes the standard one`: `(NamingTemplate "{obj1}").value` is `{obj1}`, `NamingTemplate.standard.value` is `{source}-({obj1}#{phi1}-{obj2}#{phi2})-{analyzer}-{note}`, and `KitFile.create` over step 122's id, name, author and instant holds `NamingTemplate.standard`. In `KitFileJsonTests` (step 124), whose kit file now also holds `namingTemplate = NamingTemplate "{source:CPL1=CPL,LP1=LP}-({obj1}#{phi1})-{analyzer:CPL2=CPL}"`: `a kit file round-trips through its canonical text` lists the top-level keys `author`, `created`, `id`, `modified`, `name`, `namingTemplate`, `notes`, `schemaVersion` and `sendExclude` in that order and writes the template's text verbatim as the string value of `namingTemplate`; `a schema-invalid or malformed kit file is refused before it binds` also refuses the text without `namingTemplate`, and with `namingTemplate` set to the number `7`, each with `SchemaValidationErr`. Every other kit-file fact passes unchanged.

**Acceptance.** After the kit file gains its naming template, `NamingTemplate` MUST exist in `Kit.fs` with `NamingTemplate.standard` holding 001 §J's text, `KitFile` MUST carry `namingTemplate`, `KitFile.create` MUST set the standard template and `kit.schema.json` MUST require it as a string; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a kit's naming template keeps its text, and a new kit takes the standard one` and the changed `a kit file round-trips through its canonical text` and `a schema-invalid or malformed kit file is refused before it binds`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the fifteen s27 invariants MUST pass.
